GOSUB/GOTO COMMANDS - CORTEX BASIC REV. 1.1

              2          IDT  'GOSUB'
              3  *
              4  * ROUTINE LIST:
              5  *
              6  *       GOTY            ;GOTO COMMAND
              7  *       GOSY            ;GOSUB COMMAND
              8  *       RTNY            ;RETURN COMMAND
              9  *       POPY            ;POP COMMAND
             10  *
             11  * EXTERNAL ROUTINES:
             12  *
             13          REF SFSN,CRLF,SLN
             14          REF LINE0,LINE2,LINE5,NLIN0
             15          DXOP EVFIX,11
     2F80    16  ERROR   EQU >2F80        XOP XX,14  (ERROR CALL)
     2FA0    17  ERROR2  EQU ERROR+>20
             18  *
             19  * EXTERNAL DATA:
             20  *
             21          REF ELNM        ;ERROR LINE NUMBER
             22          REF FNS         ;FOR/NEXT STACK
             23          REF GSC         ;GOSUB STACK COUNTER
             24          REF GSS         ;GOSUB STACK
             25          REF PLC         ;PROGRAM LINE COUNTER
             26          REF SLT         ;STATEMENT LOCATION TABLE
             27          REF BUS         ;BEGINNING USER STORAGE
             28          REF C4          ;>0004
             29  *
             30  * ABSTRACT:
             31  *
             32  * EXECUTE GOTO, GOSUB AND SYSTEM GOSUB COMMANDS.
             33  * PROVIDE FOR ON COMMAND
             34  *
             35  *       STACK FORMAT:   PLC
             36  *                       PBC
             37  *
             38  *                       PLC
             39  *                       PBC
             40  *
             41  *                       ...
             42  *
             43  * IF PBC = 0, GOTO NEXT LINE, OTHERWISE CONTINUE EXECUTION ON
             44  * THE SAME LINE AS THE CALL WAS MADE (NEEDED FOR ON COMMAND TO
             45  * ENSURE YOU DO NOT JUMP BACK INTO THE PARAMETER LIST.)
             46  *
             47  * CALLING SEQUENCE:
             48  *
             49  *       B @GOSB1
             50  *       B @GOSY
             51  *       B @GOTY
             52  *
             53  *       EXIT TO LINE0 IN DEMULTIPLEXOR (RUN)
             54  *
             55  * EXCEPTIONS AND CONDITIONS:
             56  *
             57  *       STACK OVERFLOW
             58  *       STACK UNDERFLOW
             59  *       NO SUCH LINE #
             60  *
